{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfukgNJKzU5DyiXhi8UsB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"No, a Worker can't listen for inbound raw TCP connections. Workers are triggered by HTTP(S) requests (plus WebSockets, cron, queues, etc.), so there's no way to bind to port 5432 and act as a Postgres server or proxy.\n\nWhat Workers can do is make *outbound* TCP connections using the `connect()` API from `cloudflare:sockets`, which is how drivers like `postgres` or `pg` talk to a database from a Worker. Cloudflare Hyperdrive builds on that for connection pooling.\n\nIf you need to accept raw TCP from clients, the usual options are Cloudflare Spectrum (Enterprise, proxies TCP to your origin) or Cloudflare Tunnel with `cloudflared access tcp` on the client side. Otherwise you'd run the proxy on a VM or container."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2263,"cache_read_input_tokens":535,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2263},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"765e981a-8b45-41b4-8f5a-0a329eacec4f","uuid":"8a1438f0-d355-427e-8654-c26bba2e5d2f","timestamp":"2026-10-11T03:39:09.836Z","request_id":"req_011CfukgN6vapZszv3Jaq7Dy"}
